U.KZ.DrinfeldAssociator.Associator.ΦN_congr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.DrinfeldAssociator.Associator.ΦN_congr","kind":"theorem","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/DrinfeldAssociator.lean#L164-L167","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.DrinfeldAssociator.Associator.ΦN","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.DrinfeldAssociator.Associator.ΦN","kind":"def","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/DrinfeldAssociator.lean#L160-L162","doc":"`Φ(A, B)` for non-resonant `A, B`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.DrinfeldAssociator.kz_Φ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.DrinfeldAssociator.kz_Φ","kind":"theorem","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/DrinfeldAssociator.lean#L148-L150","doc":"The KZ instance evaluates to `Φ_KZ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.DrinfeldAssociator.kz","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.DrinfeldAssociator.kz","kind":"def","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/DrinfeldAssociator.lean#L132-L146","doc":"**The Knizhnik–Zamolodchikov associator** as an instance of the class. Admissibility is\nnon-resonance; every law is an existing theorem about `Φ_KZ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.DrinfeldAssociator.Associator.eq_one_of_commute","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.DrinfeldAssociator.Associator.eq_one_of_commute","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/DrinfeldAssociator.lean#L117-L124","doc":"If `A` and `B` commute, `Φ(A, B) = 1`: shift `B` away to `0` (with `z = −B`), then use\nthe unit law. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.DrinfeldAssociator.Associator.isUnit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.DrinfeldAssociator.Associator.isUnit","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/DrinfeldAssociator.lean#L113-L115","doc":"`Φ(A, B)` is a unit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.DrinfeldAssociator.Associator.zero_right","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.DrinfeldAssociator.Associator.zero_right","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/DrinfeldAssociator.lean#L107-L111","doc":"`Φ(A, 0) = 1`, derived from `zero_left` and `swap_mul`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.DrinfeldAssociator.Associator.shift_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.DrinfeldAssociator.Associator.shift_left","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/DrinfeldAssociator.lean#L97-L105","doc":"Central shift on the left argument, derived from `shift_right` and `swap_mul`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.DrinfeldAssociator.Associator.Φ_congr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.DrinfeldAssociator.Associator.Φ_congr","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/DrinfeldAssociator.lean#L92-L95","doc":"`Φ` depends only on its arguments, not on the admissibility proofs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.DrinfeldAssociator.Associator.hexagon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.DrinfeldAssociator.Associator.hexagon","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/DrinfeldAssociator.lean#L83-L83","doc":"The hexagon in central form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.DrinfeldAssociator.Associator.pentagon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.DrinfeldAssociator.Associator.pentagon","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/DrinfeldAssociator.lean#L75-L75","doc":"The pentagon, in Drinfeld's coproduct form, on residues with the infinitesimal braid\nrelations. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.DrinfeldAssociator.Associator.map","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.DrinfeldAssociator.Associator.map","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/DrinfeldAssociator.lean#L69-L69","doc":"Naturality along continuous `ℂ`-algebra homomorphisms. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.DrinfeldAssociator.Associator.commute","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.DrinfeldAssociator.Associator.commute","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/DrinfeldAssociator.lean#L66-L66","doc":"Anything commuting with both arguments commutes with the associator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.DrinfeldAssociator.Associator.shift_right","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.DrinfeldAssociator.Associator.shift_right","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/DrinfeldAssociator.lean#L62-L62","doc":"Central shift on the right argument. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.DrinfeldAssociator.Associator.zero_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.DrinfeldAssociator.Associator.zero_left","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/DrinfeldAssociator.lean#L59-L59","doc":"Unit: `Φ(0, B) = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.DrinfeldAssociator.Associator.swap_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.DrinfeldAssociator.Associator.swap_mul","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/DrinfeldAssociator.lean#L55-L55","doc":"Inversion: `Φ(B, A) Φ(A, B) = 1 = Φ(A, B) Φ(B, A)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.DrinfeldAssociator.Associator.Φ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.DrinfeldAssociator.Associator.Φ","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/DrinfeldAssociator.lean#L52-L52","doc":"The associator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.DrinfeldAssociator.Associator.adm_of_nonResonant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.DrinfeldAssociator.Associator.adm_of_nonResonant","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/DrinfeldAssociator.lean#L49-L49","doc":"Every non-resonant element is admissible. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.DrinfeldAssociator.Associator.Adm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.DrinfeldAssociator.Associator.Adm","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/DrinfeldAssociator.lean#L47-L47","doc":"Admissibility of an argument. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.DrinfeldAssociator.Associator.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.DrinfeldAssociator.Associator.mk","kind":"ctor","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/DrinfeldAssociator.lean#L45-L45","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.DrinfeldAssociator.Associator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.DrinfeldAssociator.Associator","kind":"structure","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/DrinfeldAssociator.lean#L43-L86","doc":"An **evaluated Drinfeld associator**: a rule `Φ(A, B)` on admissible pairs, in every complete\nnormed `ℂ`-algebra of universe `u`, satisfying the algebraic associator laws. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.DrinfeldAssociator.ePi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.DrinfeldAssociator.ePi","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/DrinfeldAssociator.lean#L40-L41","doc":"The normalised half-twist `e^{−iπX}` used in the hexagon (the KZ normalisation). ","signatureChunk":0}]}